================================================================================
THE WEIGHT-POLYTOPE OBSTRUCTION -- a PROVED necessary condition on any GMC witness
================================================================================

 The Gaussian measure on C^K (= 2K real Gaussians) is invariant under the TORUS
        T: (A_1,...,A_K) -> (e^{i t_1} A_1, ..., e^{i t_K} A_K).
 Give the monomial prod_j A_j^{a_j} conj(A_j)^{b_j} the WEIGHT w = (a_1-b_1, ..., a_K-b_K).
 Weights ADD under multiplication, and Wick gives

        E[monomial] != 0   =>   w = 0                      (*)

 because E[A^a conj(A)^b] = delta_{ab} a!.  Two consequences, both one line:

 (1) SINGLE-WEIGHT P IS USELESS.  If every monomial of P has the same weight v != 0, then
     every monomial of Q P^m has weight w_Q + m v.  A FIXED Q has finitely many weights, so
     for large m no weight is 0 and E[Q P^m] = 0 by (*).  GMC is not refutable this way.
     (This kills the cheap 'P holomorphic' idea: holomorphic P has all weights > 0.)

 (2) THE NEWTON-WEIGHT POLYTOPE MUST CONTAIN THE ORIGIN.  If all weights of P lie in an
     OPEN half-space {w : <w,u> > 0}, then every monomial of P^m has <w,u> >= m*c with
     c = min > 0, while Q contributes a bounded shift; so again E[Q P^m] = 0 for large m.
     Hence any GMC witness needs   0 in conv(weights of P)   -- and, since a P all of whose
     weights are 0 is a polynomial in the |A_j|^2 with E[P^m] = 0 forcing P = 0 (real,
     see (3)), it needs at least one STRICTLY POSITIVE and one STRICTLY NEGATIVE weight.

 (3) REAL-VALUED P IS TRIVIAL.  If P is real-valued then E[P^2] = 0 forces P = 0 a.s.
     So GMC only has content for COMPLEX P -- which is exactly why the witness is built
     from complex combinations of the real Gaussians.

 machine check:
  known witness (1+Bb)(B-|A|^2)    weights=[(0, -1), (0, 0), (0, 1)]
     0 in hull (pos&neg present): True;  E[P^m] m=1..8 = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
     Q with E[QP^m] != 0 at large m: YES (0, 0, 0, 1)
  holomorphic A+B                  weights=[(0, 1), (1, 0)]
     0 in hull (pos&neg present): False;  E[P^m] m=1..8 = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]
     Q with E[QP^m] != 0 at large m: NO
  weight-0 |A|^2-|B|^2             weights=[(0, 0)]
     0 in hull (pos&neg present): False;  E[P^m] m=1..8 = [0, 2, 0, 24, 0, 720, 0, 40320]
     Q with E[QP^m] != 0 at large m: YES (1, 1, 0, 0)

 READING: the witness has weights {(0,1),(0,0),(0,-1)} -- straddling 0 in the B
 direction and identically 0 in the A direction.  The holomorphic and weight-0
 controls both fail exactly as (1)/(2)/(3) predict.  So the searched boxes came back
 empty for a REASON, not by accident: 2 monomials cannot straddle 0 and still kill
 every moment (P = c1 A + c2 Ab gives E[P^{2k}] = C(2k,k)(c1c2)^k k! != 0).
